NAME
     toolkitd – Daemon for indexing various actions types across the system
     into the ToolKit database

SYNOPSIS
     toolkitd

DESCRIPTION
     The toolkitd daemon indexes App Intents, SiriKit intents, shortcuts
     bundled actions and more into the ToolKit database. This database is used
     by various clients to discover and run available tools and actions.

     The daemon is launched on-demand via XPC when an indexing request is
     received.

XPC SERVICE
     toolkitd registers the Mach service com.apple.toolkitd.xpc and listens
     for ToolKitIndexingRequest messages. Upon receiving a request, it
     executes a pipeline of indexing steps to populate the tool database.

